# TBD Reforger platform

- Read [`CLAUDE.md`](/CLAUDE.md) first: the project laws, the directory atlas and the canonical
  commands. Every path in the rules is relative to the repository root.
- **HARD GATE:** [`no-silent-deferrals.mdc`](/.cursor/rules/no-silent-deferrals.mdc) — finish the
  whole ask; only the operator's explicit "defer X" defers a piece.
- **HARD GATE:** [`cursor-agent-workflow.mdc`](/.cursor/rules/cursor-agent-workflow.mdc) — which
  mode a message asks for, and when to stop and ask.
- Layout: `crates/` (crates by category and tier: the API server `crates/api/api_server/`, package
  `api_server`, over the other `crates/api/` crates; the single-page app
  `crates/frontend/shell/frontend_application/`, package `frontend_application`, Leptos and Trunk,
  over the other `crates/frontend/` crates, with the `offline_service_worker` beside it; the game
  server host agent `crates/fleet/game_server_host_agent/`; the map's streaming, rendering and GPU
  crates) · `deploy/` (Dockerfile, compose, Caddy, systemd units) · `mod/` (the Enfusion
  addons) · `tools/` (tool crates by category under `tools/<category>/`, the binaries `xtask` and
  `developer_tools`, the pinned enfusion-mcp npm package) · `contracts/` · `assets/`; the
  [workspace layout](/documentation/architecture/workspace_layout.md) describes the whole tree.
  Where a new file goes: [Where does X go?](/documentation/standards/where_does_x_go.md).
- **Keep documentation truthful.** When a change alters a folder's surface, commands or
  boundaries, update its README.md and the feature docs whose behaviour changed, and keep the
  comments of the code you alter current; this is advice, not a commit gate. Documentation lives
  in `documentation/` (entry:
  [documentation/README.md](/documentation/README.md)); its rules are in
  [documentation/standards/](/documentation/standards/README.md): the
  [documentation standards](/documentation/standards/documentation_standards.md), the
  [README standard](/documentation/standards/readme_standard.md) and the
  [commit checklist](/documentation/standards/commit_checklist.md). The code trees hold no
  Markdown but README.md files, so no application grows a documentation tree. Mission Creator documentation lives under
  [documentation/crates/frontend/workspaces/mission_creator_workspace/](/documentation/crates/frontend/workspaces/mission_creator_workspace/README.md).
- **Tickets.** Tickets, run receipts and the wave plan live in the central ticket manager, project
  `reforger`: `ttm --project reforger add` (or `add-child`) files a ticket, `show`, `brief` and
  `next` read them, and every command accepts a slug or a legacy `T-<n>` number; after a change
  run `ttm --project reforger check --strict`. `.ai/tickets/` holds the legacy ticket files only
  as data awaiting `ttm import`. The tools reach the ticket manager through
  [`ticket_manager_client`](/tools/foundation/ticket_manager_client/README.md); the wave lifecycle
  is [Running a wave](/documentation/runbooks/factory_waves/running_a_wave.md).
- **Executor gate.** A ticket's `executor` says who may take it: `claude-code` means any AI coding
  agent run through the ticket tooling, whoever makes it; `documentation` a ticket, spec or
  documentation pass; `workbench`, `human` and `ci` mean stop and wait for that party.
- **Git.** Commit directly to `main` and create no branch (`CLAUDE.md` law 2). The one exception
  is the `slice/<id>` branches that the xtask slice and wave tooling creates, merges and deletes
  itself (`cargo xtask platform slice-worktree`, `cargo xtask platform wave`,
  `cargo xtask mod wave`). A commit that lands a ticket names its id in the subject; a commit
  written with an AI agent ends with a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer; commit only when asked.
- **Factory mode.** When the operator starts the platform factory,
  [`platform-factory-mode.mdc`](/.cursor/rules/platform-factory-mode.mdc) applies and the
  orchestrating session follows
  [Factory waves](/documentation/runbooks/factory_waves/README.md).
